<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 405 mln stg late help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 405 mln stg late help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with around 405 million stg of unspecified late assistance.</p>
<p>			    EARLY	1100 GMT   1300 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    1.0 BLN	=	  1.1 BLN    1.1 BLN</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY	2 MLN	=	  342 MLN    747 MLN</p>
<p> BAND 1  BANK BILLS     2 MLN*     =	  340 MLN*   =</p>
<p> UNSPECIFIED		  =	  =	     =     405 MLN</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE - 5-11/16 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
